{
 "what": "What git was handed when a PowerShell call starts a program with Start-Process (or its aliases saps and start), command by command (FN-55, finding 0110f7). `argv` is every git started from outside git, in order, with its whole argv as git itself wrote it down (the trace2 start event, GIT_TRACE2_EVENT); an empty list: no git ran.",
 "how": "Each command was written to a .ps1 file and run by PowerShell 7 (pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File) in a scratch repository with an empty template, no hooks and nothing staged, so nothing was committed; run twice, with the same answer both times. Every case keeps its window off the desktop (-NoNewWindow or -WindowStyle Hidden) and none uses -Verb. -UseNewEnvironment is left out: git then starts without GIT_TRACE2_EVENT, so this method cannot see it.",
 "git": "git version 2.53.0.windows.1",
 "pwsh": "7.6.8",
 "powershell": "5.1.26100.9444",
 "bash": "GNU bash, version 5.2.37(1)-release (x86_64-pc-msys)",
